yTpjsTQ1eLtnUQ","review_id":"r1unSXB7KfhQ1uMveNkKoA","date":"2011-02-20T03:32:31","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9321894645690918,"text_excerpt":"This place has an exciting choice of cafe drinks. So far I've had their thai tea, espresso and an iced coconut black tea. They also have some excellent ice creams. It looks like they have some other food too, but I haven't tried that yet. This place would be good for grabbing a drink while walking around to Marigny, hanging out and doing work, meetings with small groups, and reading the Sunday paper."},{"business_id":"sy9erwW0yTpjsTQ1eLtnUQ","review_id":"ZKVWss93B2m3yxDuuVoYGg","date":"2011-03-26T05:12:33","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9279029965400696,"text_excerpt":"I love orange couch, it's easily one of my favorite coffee shops in New Orleans. And don't be worried, there is an orange couch inside for you to sit on just in case you might be wondering! I have had the coffee which was so good SO good. I have had the espresso milkshakes more than once that seriously have me craving them and going back for more. I also have had that thai tea milkshake that a friend likes to get and it's something different that was surprisingly good too! They have cute poetry slams on Wednesdays I believe with the local high/middle school kids. Overall the mod deco, the japanese ice cream, the delicious coffee, and the helpful baristas which are by the way easy on the e..."},{"business_id":"sy9erwW0yTpjsTQ1eLtnUQ","review_id":"4hX294BRwqlohx6LOxPa2w","date":"2009-12-18T20:25:05","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9251702427864075,"text_excerpt":"A hip looking (but CLEAN) coffee shop in the Marigny. I'm not a coffee drinker but their tea selection was good and tasty. Plus I got to try mochi (ice cream w/ rice something around it). Very delicious If it was in my 'hood I would be here at least once a week."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"sy9erwW0yTpjsTQ1eLtnUQ","photo_id":"xUwwBGb4FJx5zfevzFmaNA","label":"inside","image_url":"/p